# Web-first architecture

Default stack: **Next.js App Router**, **TanStack Query**, **Zustand** (or similar) for session, **shadcn/ui** + Tailwind.

## Layering (4 layers — do not add DataSource unless needed)

```text
page.tsx → useXController() → useCase() → repository.apiJson()
                ↓
           XView (presentational)
```

- **Pages** stay thin (≤ ~15 lines): wire controller, render view.
- **Views** receive a **view model** (`viewState` + `actions` or spread props); no `fetch`, no repository imports.
- **Controllers** are **`use*Controller` hooks**: React Query, form/dialog state, toasts, navigation.
- **Use cases** are **plain async functions**; map API errors to `throw new Error(...)`.
- **Repositories** are **objects or modules** calling **`apiJson`** from `@/lib/api-client`.

## Folders

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/app/` | Routes, layouts, guards |
| `src/features/<name>/` | Domain feature modules |
| `src/components/` | Shared layout + `ui/` (design system) |
| `src/lib/` | API client, env, query keys, RBAC helpers |
| `src/stores/` | Client global state (auth) |
| `src/providers/` | QueryClient, theme, i18n |

Put cross-feature logic in `src/lib/` or `src/hooks/`, not inside random features.

## From brewlab (use sparingly)

- **`route-paths` module** — single source for hrefs (avoid string drift).
- **`src/widgets/` or `src/components/forms/`** — shared field/button chrome when many screens share mobile-like inputs.
- **`FailureBus` / central toast helper** — only if error handling becomes inconsistent.

## Avoid unless requested

- Flutter-style `createAppContainer()` for every app.
- Repository interfaces + classes when a typed object + use cases suffice.
- Server Actions for all CRUD (use `apiJson` + ASP.NET/API backend pattern).
- Duplicating list state in Zustand when Query already caches it.
